# State Management

Prefer local component state when state is local.

Use feature hooks for feature-specific state.

Do not introduce a global state library unless the project genuinely requires it.

Separate:

- UI state
- drawing state
- notebook state
- application state

Do not put unrelated state into a single global store.

Avoid unnecessary state duplication.

Prefer derived values instead of storing values that can be calculated.

Keep state updates predictable and immutable.